infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Join then aggregate vs pre-aggregate then join
  desc Same orders, items, payments — the fix is collapsing each child first
  compares
    - label Join then aggregate
      children
        - label 3 × 2 = 6 rows per order
          desc Two one-to-many children fan out
        - label SUM(total) = 600
          desc True total is 100 — over-counted 6×
        - label No error raised
          desc Query runs fine and ships
        - label Passes in dev
          desc 1 item × 1 payment = 1 row hides it
    - label Pre-aggregate then join
      children
        - label 1 row per order per child
          desc Each child collapsed in a CTE/subquery
        - label SUM(total) = 100
          desc Correct — joins are one-to-one
        - label Cannot fan out
          desc Summaries join one-to-one to the parent
        - label Scales to N children
          desc Aggregate each in its own subquery
theme
  palette #f43f5e #10b981
